// REAL data. Team identity, records, and per-game stats are sourced from
// data/canonical/season=<year>/team_games.json (CFBD-derived, locked metrics).
// adjO/adjD/adjEM are AdjOff/AdjDef/AdjNet. Under the hierarchical_hfa model
// they are opponent-adjusted composites of EPA, Success Rate and
// Explosiveness, fitted with partial pooling across teams and conferences
// on garbage-time-filtered plays, and AdjNet is exactly AdjOff + AdjDef.
// Home-field advantage is fitted per metric but excluded from these
// neutral-field ratings. Under the legacy rollback model adjEM is the
// site's SRS and adjO/adjD are yards-per-play edges. CFB_RATING_MODEL
// records exactly which model produced each published season.
// Every rating is computed through each published week (no later-week games
// included). SOR (Strength of Record, sor-v1-wins-above-average)
// is wins above what an exactly-average FBS team would be expected to
// get on that same schedule -- see scripts/build_real_data.py for the
// full derivation. It answers a different question than AdjNet: résumé
// (won/lost, given the schedule) rather than performance strength, and it
// keeps its own SRS-based derivation regardless of the rating model.
// Postseason site-weeks are grouped by CFBD's own playoff round field
// (not by date gaps), so e.g. "Week 17" for a finished season is really
// one of Bowl Season / CFP First Round / Quarterfinal / Semifinal /
// National Championship -- see CFB_WEEK_LABELS for the human label.
